  Likely cause: This command adds the predicate requiring at least three users with distinct clearances. If run$8 is unsatisfiable, adding this constraint will not help. The root cause is likely the same as above: the combination of all requirements and all coverage predicates is overconstrained for the scope. It may also be that, with only 8 users, 3 roles, and 4 states, it is not possible to realize all required coverage conditions. 
  What to relax: First resolve unsatisfiability in run$8 before adding the distinct clearances predicate. If satisfied, but run$9 remains unsatisfiable, consider increasing the User or Role scope.

SATISFYING INSTANCES: Quality assessment
- 7/9 predicates yielded instances: R1, R1R2, R1R2R3, R1R2R3R4, R1R2R3R4R5, R1R2R3R4R5R6, R1R2R3R4R5R6R7.
